# Cases that reproduce bugs which were REAL. Found under generator version 1.
#
# The manifest parser originally validated member names with a blocklist
# ("/", "\", ".."), which let a Windows drive-relative name like "C:evil.ctex"
# escape the output directory. A manifest fetched from a SHARED DDC tier is
# written by another machine, so that was arbitrary file placement studio-wide.
# Fixed by replacing the blocklist with an allowlist (isPlainFilename).
#
# These seeds hit the hostile-name generator branch; they fail the CONTAINMENT
# property against the pre-fix parser.
